## Goal

Cut wasted engineering spend (cost) by ensuring every prioritization decision for this product line is backed by aggregated, evidence-weighted signal instead of anecdote or the loudest voice in the room — scoped to the transcript-to-PRD workflow for one product line.

**Primary actor:** Human + Agent co-pilot

## Trigger

Non-empty transcript pasted or uploaded, and the PM clicks Process Transcript — no minimum length or count threshold, since Juno runs per PM-initiated request, not on a background monitoring loop.

## Steps & tools

**Pattern:** Planner-Executor (multi-agent, parallel)

| Step | Action | Tool / model | Guardrail |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Plan: detect mode — strategy doc present → Strategy Mode prompt/schema; absent → Quality Mode prompt/schema. | Juno can read tickets for a given product line since a given date, read a transcript by its source ID, and look up an account's exact revenue and tier by account ID. It can read the uploaded strategy document, but only for the current session — it's never saved. And it can invoke the AI analysis call with a transcript and, optionally, a strategy document, which hands back the insights and the drafted PRD. Beyond those five reads and one invoke, it has nothing — no way to write, create, or update a ticket, a roadmap item, or any other record in this first version. | Juno can READ tickets, transcripts, the strategy document, and account ARR/tier data. It can WRITE nothing — no roadmap, ticket, or record in any connected system. The only output it produces is the insights and PRD draft shown to the PM, and only the PM's own override action can turn that into something that actually changes a system of record. |
| 2 | Execute: one structured LLM call over the full transcript (+ strategy doc if present) → returns insights + prdContent via the return_analysis tool call. | _ |  |
| 3 | Guardrail lookup: exact-match account revenue/tier lookup for any insight that would deprioritize a customer-dependent item. | _ |  |
| 4 | Normalize + render: clamp priority to P0–P3, apply safe defaults for nullable fields, group into the PRD, and pull notRecommended insights into their own section. | _ |  |

**Schemas**

Tickets come back as a list of ticket text tied to an account and a timestamp. Transcripts come back as text with a source type (interview, call, email) and a timestamp. The account lookup returns just the ARR figure and tier for one account. The strategy document read returns its raw text. And the AI analysis call returns the list of insights (each with a priority, and optionally a pillar, alignment score, rationale, and not-recommended flag) plus the drafted PRD text.

**Memory (in or out of scope)**

- **Episodic:** In-scope: transcript text, strategy document text (if loaded), mode selected, the raw model response, and the normalized insights + PRD for this run. Lifetime: end of run — cleared on the next Process Transcript click, not persisted between sessions.
- **Semantic:** In scope: the PM's override corrections (P0→P3 demotions, notRecommended reversals) aggregated into scoring calibration — lifetime: indefinite, but stored as correction patterns, not raw transcript content.

Out of scope: do not persist the strategy document itself, transcript content, or account revenue figures beyond the session — those get re-read fresh each run (matches the freshness requirement from earlier) rather than memorized, so Juno never acts on a stale strategy or an outdated ARR number.
- **Working:** In-scope: the current transcript text, the current strategy document (if loaded), detected mode, and the account revenue/tier lookups resolved for this run — held only for the duration of one Process Transcript request, then discarded.
- **External:** Support/ticketing system API (read), transcript/call-recording source (read), CRM or billing system for account ARR/tier (read), analyze-transcript edge function → AI gateway (invoke). No write access anywhere in V1 — Juno never creates or updates a ticket, roadmap item, or record on its own.

## Human-in-the-loop

PM reviews any insight flagged notRecommended before it's dropped from the roadmap, and approves any P0/P1 before it enters planning — and for the dissent guardrail specifically, control passes back whenever a decision would deprioritize something a high-ARR account depends on.

## Success & failure

- **Done when:** Success: structured { insights, prdContent } returned and normalized — hands back to the PM for review/approval.

Failure: the AI call errors, returns unparseable JSON, or omits the tool call — Juno shows nothing rather than a guess, surfaces the toast, and hands back immediately.

Escalation: any insight lands as notRecommended, or would deprioritize a high-ARR account under the dissent guardrail — hands back to the PM before it can be dropped or shipped.

Timeout: no response within the p95 latency budget (~6s) — Juno stops waiting, shows a timeout error, and hands back rather than leaving the PM staring at a spinner indefinitely.
- **Fails safe when:** Juno can READ tickets, transcripts, the strategy document, and account ARR/tier data. It can WRITE nothing — no roadmap, ticket, or record in any connected system. The only output it produces is the insights and PRD draft shown to the PM, and only the PM's own override action can turn that into something that actually changes a system of record.

